{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794843411,"nonce":"djjCNWNeqyXmUM8l3br/7uWcbu0=","title":"hxn-window in the browser: the canvas as a window, with DOM input","message":"hxnme M0. hxn-window has no wasm build. In a web page the window is the page's canvas: its size and device pixel ratio, resize, focus and visibility, and keyboard, pointer, touch, wheel, gamepad and IME composition events delivered as the same `Event` values as natively. Under Ash this runs as a browser agent that shares the canvas with the GPU agents (the claim protocol hxn-gpu-webgpu and hxn-gpu-webgl2 use); under hxcpp it is Emscripten's HTML5 events or winit's web backend.\n\nDone when hxn-window's examples run in a web page on hxcpp, threaded hxcpp and Ash, and hxn-gpu's present example takes its size and input from it.","files":null}]}